    "turn_idx": 45,
    "turn_text": "that we have, the service to the country that's really called us all to run for office, and now as we're serving, has informed our opinions of the world, I think is incredibly important. So I think a lot of us had been hearing about how the Russians attempted to influence our election system And there have been movements throughout the House to support the election system. So we've given money, you know, New Jersey. We don't have paper ballot. We're working on that. We are looking at how to ensure that voter registration is secure, how to ensure that our ballot boxes are secure, our polling places are secure. But what seems to be missing from the conversation is how the Russians used social media and used infiltrated different groups, protest groups to really create divisiveness and to influence the elections. And that's something that I think many of us have seen overseas. We've seen the Russians influence other democracies. We know what they've been doing over the past several decades. And so to come, to Congress in a time when the Russians have attempted to influence our democratic elections. There hasn't been the focus on it. You know, where is that kind of all hands-on deck to protect the 2020 election mentality that we would expect to see? And I think there was some reporting that the former Secretary of Homeland Security tried to come up with the 2020 plan for the president, and she couldn't even get that on his desk. We have taken it upon ourselves. We formed a task force century to really drill down into exactly what happened in 2016 and what the legislation should be so that we can protect 2020. Does it scare you at all that six months into the job on one of the biggest stages on earth? You are the Russia expert. Well, I don't think it's scary in the sense that we have a lot of resources and because I come from that background, no people that quite frankly have far more Russian expertise than I do, mine's a bit dated, but I think the thing that I can lean on that not everybody in the caucus can is an understanding of where to go for",
